A||||10||wkayl||Must be the week for junkyard finds...||||7||
Z||000000||wkayl||04-12-2001||09:44 PM||||OK, here's the story.  Stopped at a yard today looking for V6 parts.  I walked to where I saw a Fiero a few months ago (4-cyl).  Setting on the ground beside it was a low mileage(around 70,000) 2.8 complete.  I saw the car (86 SE) it came out of and it was hit hard in the front.  Perfect exhaust manifolds and EGR tube.  The silver wrap on the EGR tube looks new.  A few weeks ago 2 kids spent several hours pulling it out (from the top) of a car way back in the lot.  The yard stayed open after hrs. on a Fri. evening for them.  The next morning they were back.  Their mom wouldn't let them spend the $275 on his car and made him take it back and sell his car to the yard.  I didn't get any info on his car, but this coming Sat I'm going to pick the engine up for $200 minus the flywheel (clutch) , starter, and throttle body.  I'm not going to say where the yard is because I don't want anyone from Colorado to beat me back.  HE!!HE!! Mike.  <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/twocars.jpg"> ||||reg||7
Z||000001||mrfiero||04-12-2001||11:07 PM||||Actually Wayne, I did already beat you to it.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  I found this engine last Friday and was to pick it up on Monday.  Unfortunately for me I got picked for jury duty on Monday.  With my luck it was a 3 day civil trial.....with the snow storm yesterday it turned into a 4 day adventure.  I was going to go down in the morning to either get the motor or pull some stuff off of it......I guess that's what I get for doing my "civic duty".   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><BR>BTW.......that SE had 85K miles on it and the EGR tube is brand new (along with the water pump).  ||||reg||6
