Z||000006||RossT||04-13-2001||12:31 AM||||The nightly news said that Denver wash shut down with a big snow storm a couple of days ago!! First time the new airport was closed!!<BR>Did it all melt?<P>BTW we are in the 50's.  Time to break out the shorts and take the t-tops off.<P>Also glad to see you are posting again!!<P>[This message has been edited by RossT (edited 04-13-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by RossT (edited 04-13-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||mrfiero||04-13-2001||01:30 AM||||Ross,<P>One of the GREAT things about Colorado is the weather.  One day can be a blizzard and the next day you're in shorts getting a sunburn.  We got about a foot of snow Tuesday night/Wednesday morning and by Thursday afternoon it was all gone.  In fact, it was so nice today that (after we "hung 'em at the courthouse) I took the GT out for a spin.<P>BTW....the trial involved a motorcycle/car accident.  The bike rider was suing the cars driver for damages suffered in the wreck.  I learned a lot about the judicial system and why I will never get on a motorcycle! <P>Without going into the particulars.....motorcycle insurance (at least in Colorado) doesn't cover ANY medical bills incurred by the driver of said motorcycle.  We're a "no fault" state and it does not apply to motorcycles......this is why the cyclist was suing.  I also found out that any traffic tickets issued were not admissable as evidence (at least in this case).  After it was all over we sided with the defendant (the car driver) as the plaintiff just didn't prove their case.  Afterwards we talked with the car driver & his attorney and discovered that the bike driver had no license, was wearing no helmet and was cited for running a red light.......all of this wasn't admitted in as evidence!  Very interesting.<P>So Wayne.....where is that motor going?  Are you putting it in the Formula or ???  <P>Ross.....I really envy you with those T-Tops.  I miss my T-Top Formula (I guess I'll have to get another one!)   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000008||RossT||04-13-2001||01:45 AM||||Mrfiero, Very interesting info.  Sound like you guys made the correct decisions.<P>Actually my fiero is up on stands.  I dropped the tank to fix that pesky sending unit. 12 year old gas and sending units don't mix.  I took it apart, sanded the varnish of it, adjusted the ohms, and now I know how much gas I have left.  I then added gas in 2 gallon increments to see the corresponding readings on the gauge.<P>While we are off topic, What ever happened to you last speeding ticket? <P>What about that move to Las Vegas?<P>Finally, did you every get the TA?<P>Good to hear the snow is gone there!!<P>Ross||||reg||1
Z||000009||mrfiero||04-13-2001||01:58 AM||||I hear you on the sending units......you should see what the ones off of the cars I got from Fiero Dave looked like!  Yours at least had the benefit of being stored indoors.<P><BR>Now to answer your questions......    <P>I go to court myself on May 10th for my little traffic ticket.....wish me luck!<P>The Las Vegas move may or may not still happen.....either way it will have to wait until after May 10th.<P>I haven't gotten the T/A yet.  In fact, I may just pass on it......I haven't figured that out yet.  I may just start driving the GT a little more and save the $23K for something else.  If I do I will need to find another set of GT+4's.....mine are pretty hard (I can spin my tires from a start without trying.....and it's an auto.!).<P>I'm glad the snow is gone too!  It's pretty rare for us to get that much on April.  Plus it was a VERY wet & heavy snow, which is what caused most of the problems (some people are still without electricity).<P>Talk to you later.    <p>[This message has been edited by mrfiero (edited 04-13-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000010||wkayl||04-13-2001||12:14 PM||||The engine is going into my shed (with 3 Fieros on the road with 2.8s you never know when it will come in handy).  The EGR tube is going on my GT and my EGR tube is going on my son's GT (I had patched his with JB weld).  The exhaust manifolds are going on Dnyee's Formula.  I think I'm going to put the water pump on My car also.  I have 92,000 miles on it now and plan on taking a couple of 2,000 mile trips this summer.||||reg||1
